# The scanner is faithful to the reference, and the reference's flex rule is
# `[ \t\v\n\f]` — there is no carriage return in it. A CRLF checkout therefore
# turns every script into "unrecognized token" on its first line, which is what
# the first Windows CI run found in `crates/engine-sim-cli/tests/cli_tests.rs`.
#
# Whether the *product* should accept CRLF is a separate question (the original
# refuses it, so accepting it is a deliberate divergence); this keeps the
# repository's own assets identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.mr      text eol=lf
*.trace   text eol=lf
*.graph   text eol=lf
*.values  text eol=lf
*.execute text eol=lf
*.errors  text eol=lf
